  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1151 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nBroad upper level troughing continues to engulf eastern CONUS\ntoday while areas out west remain influenced by upper level\nridging. Given this synoptic layout, the Mid-South sits in prime\nposition for reinforcing frontal passages. As such, the next\nboundary will impact the area this afternoon. Cool and dry air\nwill filter in behind, allowing overnight lows to span the upper\n20s to mid 30s. Much cooler conditions are anticipated Friday\nthrough the weekend as highs stay in the low to mid 50s. An\nareawide freeze is forecast Saturday morning. Areas in west\nTennessee will see the chillest temperatures as lows dip into the\nupper 20s. Below normal temperatures will continue into early\nnext week.\n\nOn Sunday, an upper level low will develop east of the Rockies\nand trek southeast. The track of this system varies between\ndeterministic guidance with the ECMWF favoring a more northerly\nplacement of the low. Regardless of track, precipitation will be\ndissuaded by the presence of dry air. A few drops may make it to\nthe surface in the Mississippi Delta Sunday night. However, no\nappreciable rainfall is forecast. Dry conditions will persist\nthrough the remainder of next week, likely worsening the current\ndrought. Otherwise, expect next week to be pleasant with highs\nreturning to the 60s by midweek.",
